WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.213
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.213 --> 00:00:02.190
(gun shooting)

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:04.490
- [Narrator] Online
multiplayer games would become

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:06.200
a pretty big deal.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.960
- [Man] Death match and online
gameplay changed everything.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.270
- [Gamer 1] Whoa! What?!

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:12.103
- [Gamer 2] Agh!

00:00:12.103 --> 00:00:14.140
- [Narrator] Players could
connect over a network and

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:16.053
interact.
- [Gamer] Look at the death!

00:00:16.053 --> 00:00:17.954
- [Narrator] Immersing
themselves in a new world,

00:00:17.954 --> 00:00:18.870
- [Gamer] Boom!

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.270
- [Narrator] but with each other.

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:22.660
- [Man] For the first time,
you can play at a high speed

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:26.470
3d world, where you're
blowing your friends apart.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:27.503
- [Gamer] God damn it.

00:00:27.503 --> 00:00:28.336
(laughter)

00:00:28.336 --> 00:00:30.130
- It's really fun to play
against each other in

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.300
death match.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.850
And to influence everybody
in wanting to make games.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:38.100
- [Narrator] And then the
guys at ID handed players

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.080
the keys to their kingdom

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.750
- [Man] We fully open the game.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.970
Then we gave out the information

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:46.200
on the way that levels were created.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.700
- [Narrator] DOOM was
opened up to modding.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:51.010
Tech savvy players could now replace the

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:54.150
existing characters,
sound effects, textures

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:57.380
you name it with their own creations.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:59.290
- [Man] People are starting
to make new graphics,

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:01.763
new weapons, new sounds for stuff.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.610
It was basically everything that you see

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:05.960
in the game can be changed,

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:09.500
but we didn't allow anyone to modify DOOM

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.924
if they didn't buy it.

00:01:10.924 --> 00:01:11.757
(laughing)

00:01:11.757 --> 00:01:13.210
So if you have the
shareware version of DOOM

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:16.220
you can't run levels or mods or anything.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:18.230
So that was actually kind of a way

00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:20.893
of forcing people to buy it.

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:25.440
But also players want to be creative.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.610
It's a lot easier to modify them than

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:29.580
to try and make a whole new thing.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:32.780
So letting people mod a game
kind of gives them a taste

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.400
of what it's like to make a game,

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.240
and now the game, you
know, fits them better.

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:38.560
- [Narrator] DOOM was put in the hands

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:41.420
of players, and they made it their own.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:43.393
- The game lives on forever.

